          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000029\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"A clear access problem leads Juniper to stock Pip and redirect the parade; the lane full of open books gives the story a warm, concrete close.\"},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Juniper’s discovery that the covered bundles are books changes the mayor’s plan, ending vividly with children reading together in the square.\"},{\"id\":\"s000047\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"The empty cart and inaccessible lane create a meaningful problem, resolved through a mobile library and a strongly visual final image.\"},{\"id\":\"s000073\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"The competing promise and quiet-reader invitation are reconciled thoughtfully: Bram gives away the bell and makes a ribbon-silent parade.\"},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The quiet-parade solution is appealing and the ending is concrete, but the events are noticeably reordered: the ribbons are tied before Bram agrees to forgo the bell.\"},{\"id\":\"s000043\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Gentle imagery and a satisfying silent-library ending work well, though the cart is prepared with ribbons before the discussion that motivates that choice.\"},{\"id\":\"s000068\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The outreach premise and lane ending are strong, but Pip is loaded and decorated before Mayor Mallow accepts the redirected route, softening the causal sequence.\"},{\"id\":\"s000096\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Books becoming the parade makes a clear turn and a lovely reading-centered ending, though the banner is attached before the packed books are discovered.\"},{\"id\":\"s000005\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Juniper identifies readers who cannot reach the square and brings books to them, with polished child-friendly imagery and a complete visual resolution.\"},{\"id\":\"s000085\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":4,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The quiet procession has graceful imagery, but the key resolution is missing: Bram’s bell promise is introduced and never shown being fulfilled or consciously changed.\"}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":5,\"causal_path\":4,\"ending\":4,\"language\":5,\"overall\":4},\"diversity_evidence\":\"This sample contains three materially different problem frames: reaching isolated lane readers (s000029, s000047, s000068, s000005), recognizing books wrongly treated as decorations (s000057, s000096), and reconciling a bell promise with quiet guests (s000073, s000034, s000043, s000085). Within each frame, however, stories are duplicates or near-duplicates, and all resolve in a book-cart parade ending with readers and open books. The evidence reflects only this sample, not the entire generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"story_ids\":[\"s000029\",\"s000047\",\"s000068\",\"s000005\"],\"summary\":\"Juniper redirects a grand parade to a narrow lane, fills the empty cart with books, and brings reading to people unable to reach the square.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000057\",\"s000096\"],\"summary\":\"The mayor mistakes bundled books for decorations; Juniper reveals their true purpose, and the parade becomes a book-sharing event.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000073\",\"s000034\",\"s000043\",\"s000085\"],\"summary\":\"A ringing bell parade conflicts with invited quiet readers; the intended solution replaces noise with ribbons, although s000085 omits the bell-promise resolution.\"}]}",
